omments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-09-26T13:46:15Z"},{"number":494,"title":"Tried on AWS ec2?","comments":1,"category":"General","created_at":"2026-09-20T19:41:44Z"},{"number":480,"title":"how to sign in to iCloud","comments":0,"category":"General","created_at":"2026-09-19T17:17:57Z"},{"number":455,"title":"Windows support or a Windows-compatible alternative?","comments":2,"category":"General","created_at":"2026-09-07T10:00:28Z"},{"number":449,"title":"Apple intelligence supported?","comments":0,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-08-29T07:47:55Z"},{"number":444,"title":"Mobile Application security testing","comments":0,"category":"General","created_at":"2026-08-25T13:37:20Z"}],"latest_release":{"name":"vphone 2.17.1","tag":"2.17.1","published_at":"2026-11-13T09:01:22Z","body":"## vphone 2.17.1\n\nA patch release of the changes merged since 2.17.0. Launchpad 2.17 and `VPhone.bundle` 2.17.x stay interchangeable; the minimum bundle is unchanged.\n\n**Core Bundle**\n\n- iPad: the framebuffer stays panel-native, so the pointer is drawn in landscape too (`dyld-cfw-quartzcore_unrotated_framebuffer`). (#926)\n- ARM64E_X1: the 35 remaining standalone accessibility plug-ins, including UIKit and SwiftUI, are lowered like the debug libraries. This fixes apps faulting in `+[AXUIKitPopGlue initialize]` at startup on hosts without FEAT_PAuth_LR when accessibility is on. Each plug-in is its own patch, on in Standard and off in the tvOS, HomePod, HomeView, watchOS and visionOS presets; an image that needs no lowering is left untouched. (#924)\n- New read-only `vphone-cli cfw audit-arm64e-x1 <volume root>` reports standalone X1 libraries and plug-ins that still need lowering, with `--json` and `--strict`. (#924)\n\n**Launchpad**\n\n- Version only; the helper is unchanged, so its build stays 21.\n\n**Upgrading**\n\nUpdate the environment of an existing machine (`vphone-cli cfw update-environment`) to apply the new patches; no restore is needed.\n","is_prerelease":false}